   "The firm forecasts the Fed could reduce its balance sheet by $1.5 trillion over the coming years.",
   "Key levers for reduction include drawing down the Treasury General Account (TGA) by $0.5 trillion and adjusting terms for foreign official institution reverse-repo holdings currently at $350 billion.",
   "The Fed may shift to an 'ample-reserves' framework requiring significantly fewer reserves by adjusting interest on reserve balances (IORB) and easing liquidity coverage ratio (LCR) constraints.",
   "Treasury issuance of short-term bills can absorb the supply of Treasuries shed by the Fed, preventing a significant rise in aggregate duration risk.",
